<title>UK: Thomson directories sold for 80 million stg.</title>
<headline>Thomson directories sold for 80 million stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomson Directories Ltd said on Wednesday that owners US WEST International had sold it for 80 million stg to a group backed by 3I.  </p>
<p>The consortium includes members of the Thomson management team, headed by Gary List, its chief executive.</p>
<p>Thomson, launched in 1980, is one of the largest independent classified directory publishers in the world. It publishes 164 area editions of its Thomson Local directory across the UK.</p>
<p>More than 20 million copies are distributed free-of-charge by the company annually, reaching 80 percent of all UK households and businesses.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
